      "data": {
        "text": "**Selecting Cloud Vision AI**\n\nI've decided to proceed with Google Cloud Vision AI for text detection within the Python script. I want to make sure the user is able to easily identify this external provider in the code.\n\n\n**Choosing Vision AI Provider**\n\nI'm now zeroing in on the file structure and specific implementation details. The plan is to create `detect_image_text.py` and integrate the Google Cloud Vision AI client. I will define a function that will take image data and make the text extraction. I am focusing on making the provider's integration clear, specifically through the import of the `google.cloud.vision` client. I'll need to remember to focus the function's return to the extracted text, nothing else.\n\n\n**Implementing Text Detection**\n\nI'm solidifying the `detect_image_text.py` structure. The function, `detect_text_from_image`, will handle either an image path or content for flexibility. I'm focusing on a clean integration of the `google-cloud-vision` library, ensuring the API client is correctly initialized within the function. My key focus is on retrieving and returning the precise text extracted.\n\n\n",
        "time": {
