      "data": {
        "text": "**Choosing Cloud Vision AI**\n\nI've decided to proceed with Google Cloud Vision AI for image label detection. The next step is to solidify how to integrate it within the `detect_image_labels.py` script, which will include adding and testing the necessary API calls. I also need to make sure the key elements are set up.\n\n\n**Defining the Implementation**\n\nNow I have a clearer outline for the `detect_image_labels.py` script. I've mapped out the essential steps. I'll import the vision library from google.cloud and set up a function, `detect_labels`, to take an image path. Inside, I'll instantiate the ImageAnnotatorClient, load the image, create a Vision image object, and use the client for label detection. Lastly, I'll process and return the detected labels.\n\n\n",
        "time": {
          "end": 1789860440751,
          "start": 1789860439284
        },
        "type": "reasoning"
      },
      "id": "prt_0bbfee4f4001s73ETC5WgEKKAX",
